        <item>
            <title>0.5.4</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:03:37 +0300</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/tvidenov/AgentDock-releases/releases</link>
            <sparkle:version>35</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<p><strong>Codex app threads open where they are.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Clicking a Codex app thread opens that thread</strong> in the Codex app, from the strip or an Inbox card.</li><li><strong>Threads in the current Codex app are recognised as the app's.</strong> It now runs them through a copy of the Codex CLI it carries inside, so AgentDock took them for a terminal session and clicking did nothing.</li><li>Release notes are back: 0.5.2 and 0.5.3 went out without them.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Also new since 0.5.1:</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>⌘-click an agent</strong> on the strip to go straight to it, and choose in Settings › General what a plain click does. Inbox cards have a button that takes you to the agent.</li><li><strong>Settings is in tabs</strong> at one size, with <strong>Settings › Apps</strong>: what works in each app and terminal, how to set it up, and whether it's ready on this Mac.</li></ul>
]]></description>
